%n ka[ppa]ki lū šebir
#note: Many of the previous editors of Adapa understand the verb as @i{lušebbir} “I will break”. However, as the verb occurs in the G stem elsewhere in this composition (l. 12’, l. 49’) when a transitive meaning is implied, the form is here taken as a precative stative “it shall be broken”. This is also how @bib{Dietrich_AOAT42@43} and @bib{RN1982@254} understand the form.
// cf. (Adapa Sum. Meturan 65a)

%n kīma ina pîš[u i]qbû ša [šū]ti kappaša ittešbir
// cf. L I.7 SB "-" b+11
// cf. (Adapa Sum. Meturan 111-112)

