// cf. L I.7 SB "-" c+3
// cf. (Adapa Sum. Meturan 132-135)

%n ea ša šamê idī ilpus[s]ū-ma
#note: @akk{i-di} is here taken to be an obl. dl. form of @i{idu} “side, arm” in accordance with the interpretation brought forward by @bib{RN552@431}, who translates “Hier berührte der ‘Ea des Himmels’ [ihm] die Arme”. Most other editors of the text understand it as a form of @i{idû} “to know”. To circumvent the problem of the missing subjunctive ending, @bib{RN216@185}, @bib{Dietrich_AOAT42@46} and @bib{RN303@117} interpret @i{ša šamê} as “the things/ways of heaven” and translate the whole phrase as a parenthesis. @bib{RN164@527} also seems to follow their interpretation (“the ways of heaven”), yet still chooses to translate the phrase (more freely) as a relative clause.
// cf. (Adapa Sum. Meturan 136-136a)

